creating:
What phantoms fill the dimly lighted room;
What ghostly shades in awe-creating guise
Are bodied forth within the teeming gloom.

creeds:
I think it brave and grand;
When men of diverse sects and creeds
Are clasping hand in hand.

crease:
Ain't seen no sich fancy dressin' sence las' quah'tly meetin' day;
Gals all dressed in silks an' satins, not a wrinkle ner a crease,
Eyes a-battin', teeth a-shinin', haih breshed back ez slick ez grease;

creed:
Work gently, sun and rain;
She held it as her dying creed
That she would grow again.

creep:
And all my cheerless orisons are sung;
Let me depart, with faint limbs let me creep
To some dim shade and sink me down to sleep.

creature's:
Infinite Love where'er we turn our eyes
Appears: this ev'ry creature's wants supplies;
This most is heard in Nature's constant voice,

creamy:
To eye the comely milking maid
Herself so fresh and creamy:
'Good day to you,' at last I said;

cressid:
And Sappho is a roving dust;
Cressid could love again; Dido,
Rotted in state, is restless still:
